WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.300
We have a lot of choices
to make about our diet.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.180
Add to that, doing
the right thing

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.380
when it comes
to preventing

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.700
and treating a
chronic disease,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.040
fighting a virus,
or losing weight,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.440
and suddenly our
nutrition choices

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.840
can seem almost
overwhelming.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.240
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.460
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.560
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.560
It’s time for the
Nutrition Facts Grab Bag

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.140
where we look at the science
on a whole variety of topics.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.380
Today, we start with
an unusual finding.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.020
Did you know that
burning incense

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.000
has been found to generate
about four times

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.280
the particulate matter
as burning cigarettes?

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.840
Here’s the story.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.220
Frankincense and myrrh date
back to thousands of years

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.780
before the three wise men.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.880
The burning of witch's incense

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.820
may have actually had
a hygienic functions,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.660
like maybe repelling mosquitoes,
and when put to the test,

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.760
incense fumes were able to kill off

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.440
some bacteria and mold in the air

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.680
but may also carry health risks.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.100
Although the adverse health effects
of second-hand tobacco smoke

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.460
are well recognized, the impact
of burning incense in the home

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.880
has received less attention, but
burning incense has been found

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.540
to generate like four times the
particulate matter as cigarettes;

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.520
so, incense may be even worse!

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.720
No wonder home incense use
may have significant adverse

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.700
health effects, particularly
on the heart and lungs,

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.560
including childhood asthma.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.040
No wonder, since the incense
smoke particle size

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.840
peaks down in the danger range,
so ultrafine they can float

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.060
down into the deepest
parts of the lungs.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.540
It’s not just the little ash
particles in the smoke though,

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.140
there’s carbon monoxide, nitric
oxides, sulfur dioxide,

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.200
carcinogenic polycyclic
aromatic hydrocarbons,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.520
and volatile organic compounds
like benzene and formaldehyde.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.600
The World Health Organization suggests
limiting indoor formaldehyde

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.960
to about 80 parts per billion,
but even with a window open

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.360
during the hour or so
incense is burning,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.960
formaldehyde levels
exceed the safety limit.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.560
What does this all mean in
terms of disease outcomes?

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.360
Studies on rats show incense can
do all sorts of terrible things,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.040
but what about people?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.240
A study of thousands of children
followed over time found

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.360
that exposure to household
incense burning was associated

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.680
with impaired lung function,
reduced lung function growth,

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.340
and increased risks of
respiratory diseases and symptoms.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.880
Daily exposure is associated
with impaired lung function

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.540
in adolescents too, though
interestingly those who had

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.180
pets at home appeared to
have better lung function.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.440
Something I noted previously, how
having a dog or cat in the house

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.400
during early life may protect against
childhood asthma and allergy.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.380
What about the heart?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.800
Long-term exposure to incense
burning in the home environment

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.460
was associated with an increased
risk of cardiovascular mortality.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.580
Approximately 8 percent of
heart disease deaths and

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.640
12 percent of stroke deaths could
potentially be attributed

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.380
to incense use, though they were
looking at long-term exposure,

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.540
so like incense burning at home on
a daily basis for more than 20 years.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.940
What about cancer?

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.720
Temple workers exposed to incense
day in and day out were found

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.780
to have evidence of
signiﬁcantly more DNA damage,

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.360
including DNA strand breaks.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.480
Does this translate
into greater cancer risk?

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.640
One unsolved mystery has been
why non-smoking Asian women

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.500
have such high lung cancer rates.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.300
Might it be incense?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.380
Probably not, since the
association between incense use

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.540
and lung cancer
remains inconclusive,

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.720
though incense use does
appear to be linked to cancers

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:49.860
of the upper respiratory tract,
as well as brain tumors

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.280
among children whose mother
were exposed to incense.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.480
Three times the odds, even more
than that of second-hand smoke.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.380
In fact, even more than the
consumption of bologna sandwiches.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.080
Processed meat consumption
only appears to at most

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.660
double brain tumor
risk among children.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.160
Even without tumors, a study of
15,000 infants found that

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.160
household incense burning
was associated with a delay

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.700
in brain development milestones
such as when they start to walk.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.100
And then on the other
side of the life cycle,

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.940
incense exposure among older adults
was associated with reduced

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.380
cognitive performance and adverse
structural changes in the brain.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.740
The researchers conclude that
this calls for safer practices,

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.380
such as avoiding
burning incense indoors

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.840
or using safer incense alternatives.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.680
So-called environmentally friendly
types of incense have been

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.600
put to the test, and…

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.900
they were found to contain
even higher concentrations

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:50.340
of several potentially carcinogenic
polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.520
Despite being a
recognized health hazard,

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.700
burning incense remains
in widespread use.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.540
In the very least, we may want to
avoid burning incense in the home

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.120
when susceptible
individuals are present,

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.820
such as the very young,
the very old, or

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.700
people with a family history of
allergy or pre-existing

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.160
cardiovascular or respiratory disease.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.140
One innovative suggestion
is electronic incense,

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.200
like the e-cigarette
of the incense world,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.880
so you can get the fragrance

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.580
without the combustion
by-products of smoke.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.140
Most of the concern about
e-cigarette-related adverse events

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.480
traditionally have revolved
around the nicotine,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.520
which wouldn’t be a
problem with e-incense,

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.420
the concern that e-cigarette use
would lead to real cigarette use.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:41.160
But now that there have been
thousands of cases of lung injury

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.720
associated with vaping, and
we’re still actually not sure

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.520
what’s causing the issue,

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.980
it seems to me we
should figure that out

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:54.180
before we push for the
electronic incense equivalent.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.300
One option in the meantime
is scented candles,

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.640
which, under normal
conditions of use,

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.600
do not appear to pose known
health risks to the consumer.

00:06:04.593 --> 00:06:06.840
Next up, we look
at specific foods

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.700
that have shown in
randomized controlled trials

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.369
to improve symptoms
like hot flashes.

00:06:11.596 --> 00:06:13.620
There is a great
variety of symptoms

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.720
suffered by women
undergoing menopause.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.360
There are the so-called
vasomotor symptoms,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.380
like night sweats and hot
ﬂashes, diﬃculty sleeping

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:26.040
or full-on insomnia, vaginal
dryness, and pain during sex,

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.640
as well as adverse effects on mood
including full-blown depression.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.740
Might exercise help?

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.280
Exercise can certainly help with
physical and psychological quality

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.160
of life in general, but unfortunately
there was no evidence

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.580
for the eﬀects of exercise on
menopause-speciﬁc symptoms.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.540
You know researchers are
getting desperate when they try

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.480
to see if giving people
pig placenta will help.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.300
Spoiler alert: it doesn’t.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.440
Well, we know oxidative stress,
which is a consequence of

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.100
excessive free oxygen radicals
or impaired antioxidant defense,

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.840
is linked not only to diseases

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.020
such as diabetes, obesity,
and cardiovascular disease,

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.900
but also menopausal
symptoms like hot flashes.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.260
Low free oxygen radical
defense is associated with

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.500
more menopausal symptoms,
just like having a diet with more

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.680
antioxidants is associated
with fewer menopausal symptoms.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:20.160
In fact, a high intake of
fruits and vegetables may delay

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.200
the onset of menopause
in the first place,

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.780
thought to be because
the presence of antioxidants

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.240
in fruits and vegetables may
counteract the adverse effects

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:30.300
of free radicals on the number
of functional eggs you still have

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:33.360
in your ovaries, whereas
a reason high meat consumption

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.760
has been related to
degenerative diseases

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.460
may not just be the
saturated fat and cholesterol,

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.600
but the pro-oxidation products
generated during their production,

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.320
storage, digestion,
and metabolism of meat.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.860
Similarly, since a pro-
inflammatory diet has also been

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.680
associated with higher menopause-
specific somatic symptoms,

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.140
meaning like hot flashes
and sleep issues,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.800
that would mean moving
towards a more plant-based diet

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.800
packed with anti-inflammatory
components like fiber

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.440
and away from pro-inflammatory
foods containing

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:05.820
saturated fat and cholesterol.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.760
No wonder whole plant
foods intake has been

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.040
associated with fewer
menopausal symptoms.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:16.200
In terms of specific foods,
poultry and skim dairy products

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.200
may be particularly bad,
whereas soy milk seemed to help.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.080
So, women may derive benefit
from lower consumption

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.840
of poultry and skimmed dairy
and a greater consumption

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.100
of vegetables and soy milk.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.700
You don’t really know, though...
until you put it to the test.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.820
And indeed, women randomized
to drink soy milk reduced

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.480
their menopausal symptoms by
20 percent within 12 weeks.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.780
No wonder that those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:41.820
report less bothersome
menopausal symptoms.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.040
Among women undergoing menopause,

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.680
vegans reported less
bothersome symptoms,

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.720
and within the diet
groups more vegetables,

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.020
and in the meat-eating group,
less ﬂesh food was associated

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.060
with less bothersome
symptoms as well.

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.880
So, eating a plant-based
diet may be helpful for women

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.900
in their menopausal transition
who prefer a natural means

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.660
to manage their symptoms,
consistent with all the other

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.780
studies demonstrating reduced
menopausal symptoms in those

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.160
consuming greater quantities of
plant-based foods and less meat.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.980
But again, maybe
there are other reasons

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.840
healthier eaters
have fewer symptoms.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:22.080
You can’t prove cause and
effect until...you guessed it.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.540
An interventional trial to
see if changing your diet

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.860
actually reduces symptoms.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.640
And in this study, where women
were encouraged to decrease fat

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.800
and increase fruit, vegetable,
and whole grain intake,

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:35.400
they were significantly
more likely to eliminate

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.520
their vasomotor symptoms like
hot flashes and night sweats

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.260
compared to the control group.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.420
So, it’s certainly not all or nothing.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:45.780
And within a plant-based
diet, those randomized

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:48.660
to a meat-free diet with
daily flaxseed oil, walnuts,

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:50.850
and almonds did better
than those randomized

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.880
to the same diet but with
daily extra-virgin olive oil.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.240
After 16 weeks, the
vegetarian diet that was rich

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:01.260
in omega-3s did better reducing
vasomotor symptom frequency.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.680
In fact, even just two teaspoons
worth of ground flaxseeds a day

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:09.120
alone can significantly decrease
menopausal symptoms to about

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.820
the same extent as
hormone replacement therapy,

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.340
but without the side effects.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.160
Finally today,
we have more info

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:22.432
on that fabulous spice fenugreek
and how it can help control blood sugar.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:25.680
The spice fenugreek is
considered to be one of

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:29.340
humanity’s oldest medicinal plants.
What can it do?

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:33.000
In my last video on fenugreek,
I explored the evidence showing

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.760
it can improve sexual
function in both men and women,

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:37.680
decrease menstrual pain,

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.680
and boost milk production
in lactating mothers.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.720
And what are the side effects?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.960
Fifteen randomized controlled
trials show, on average,

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:49.740
a significant improvement
in cholesterol levels.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:52.500
And a dozen other studies show
significant improvements

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.740
in both long- and short-term blood
sugar control in diabetics

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.760
and prediabetics using an average of
about a half teaspoon a day

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.760
over a period of an
average of two months.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.780
Results clearly indicate that
fenugreek is an inexpensive,

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.360
low-risk dietary supplement
that has potential

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:11.880
to improve blood sugar
control in diabetes.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:16.560
What exactly is the mechanism by
which it lowers blood sugars?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.940
There’s a peculiar amino
acid in fenugreek

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:24.660
that increases insulin
release from the pancreas.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.400
The peculiar 4-hydroxyisoleucine
has been described as

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:33.000
an efﬁcient compound in the
regulation of insulin secretion.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.760
Due to the fact that it
acts as a secretagogue

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:39.120
in the presence of elevated
blood glucose concentrations,

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.000
it has been proposed for
the potential treatment

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.080
of insulin resistance,
diabetes, and obesity.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:50.760
There’s a class of diabetes drugs
that does the same thing:

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.880
sulfonylureas, sold as like glucotrol,

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.340
glyburide, micronase, glipizide.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.580
The problem is that they
increase insulin secretion

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.500
whether you need it or not,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.040
and so there’s a risk
of severe hypoglycemia,

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.260
driving your blood sugars too low.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:10.980
The funky fenugreek amino
acid, on the other hand,

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.960
only boosts it when you need it.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.420
When your blood sugars are
normal, it has no effect.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.120
It only seems to stimulate
extra insulin release

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:21.180
when you need it most, when
your blood sugars are high.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:24.720
What these researchers did,
was after consent was obtained

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.480
from family members,
pancreases were obtained

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.520
from brain-dead organ donors.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.280
Put the insulin-secreting
cells in a petri dish

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.260
at a low blood sugar concentration,

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:36.060
and they release a little insulin,

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:38.940
and at high blood sugar levels
they release more insulin.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.340
That makes sense.
That’s what they’re supposed to do,

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.680
since insulin is the
hormone your body releases

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.960
when trying to bring
down your blood sugars.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.380
Add in some of that
fenugreek amino acid, though,

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:52.260
and you can boost insulin
production. Great!

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:56.160
But if that happened even at the
low blood sugar concentration too,

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.500
it would be like the drugs
and you could dip too low,

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.360
but no, when you don’t need extra
insulin, no fenugreek effect.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.060
What about the role of fenugreek

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.820
in the prevention of type 2 diabetes?

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:12.360
A 3-year randomized controlled
study of the efficacy

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.840
of fenugreek on men and women
diagnosed with prediabetes.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:19.380
Those randomized to fenugreek
were told to take about

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:22.080
one and a third teaspoons of
fenugreek powder twice a day

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.480
before meals, and both the fenugreek

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.000
and the control groups that
didn’t get any fenugreek

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.400
were both given identical
diet and lifestyle advice.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:33.300
And, by the end of the study,
the cumulative incidence rate

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:37.320
of diabetes was reduced significantly
in the fenugreek group.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:40.980
Check it out. Those who didn’t
get the fenugreek

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:44.220
had a four times higher
chance of developing diabetes,

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.760
and you could already see
the groups starting to diverge

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.480
within six months, and all
from just a few cents worth

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:54.124
of a spice, every day.

